# Flow: PUSH · Firebase Cloud Messaging (fcm)
#
# A complete flow on its own tenant: create the tenant, add the provider, (template),
# send, check which provider and From delivered it.
#
# Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client): click "Send Request"
# above each request, top to bottom. Ids and the API key are taken from earlier responses
# automatically. Replace <...> values in bodies with your own (passwords, tokens).
# {{name}}-style placeholders inside template bodies are Handlebars for the hub: REST Client
# sends them as they are (it may underline them as unknown variables; that is fine).
# No REST Client? Copy the method, URL, headers and JSON body into Swagger/Postman.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@opsUrl = http://localhost:9464
# ADMIN_API_KEY from your .env
@ADMIN_KEY = paste-your-ADMIN_API_KEY-here
# FCM registration token from your app (push / in-app only)
@FCM_TOKEN = paste-a-device-token-here

### 1 · Check the service is ready
# Expect {"ready":true}. If 503, start Postgres/Redis.
# @name r1_check_the_service_is_ready
GET {{opsUrl}}/health/ready

### 2 · Create a tenant for this flow
# Admin creates a tenant just for this flow (so only this provider is configured); starter templates
# otp + welcome are added; the API key is returned once. Already ran this flow? Change the slug (409
# TENANT_SLUG_TAKEN).
# @name r2_create_a_tenant_for_this_flow
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/admin/tenants
Content-Type: application/json
x-admin-key: {{ADMIN_KEY}}

{
  "name": "Acme Inc.",
  "slug": "acme-push-demo",
  "settings": { "appName": "Acme" }
}

### 3 · Add the Firebase provider
# Paste the whole Firebase service account JSON (Firebase console → Project settings → Service
# accounts → Generate key) as ONE string. Encrypted, cached in Redis, used by push and in-app.
# @name r3_add_the_firebase_provider
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/providers
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{r2_create_a_tenant_for_this_flow.response.body.$.apiKey.key}}

{
  "channel": "CHANNEL_PUSH",
  "provider": "fcm",
  "name": "firebase",
  "priority": 1,
  "credentials": {
    "service_account": "{\"type\":\"service_account\",\"project_id\":\"acme-app\",\"private_key_id\":\"<PRIVATE_KEY_ID>\",\"private_key\":\"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\\n<KEY>\\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\\n\",\"client_email\":\"firebase-adminsdk@acme-app.iam.gserviceaccount.com\"}"
  }
}

### 4 · Register the user's device
# Your backend sends the token your app got from the Firebase SDK. Pushes with userId go to every
# active token of the user.
# @name r4_register_the_user_s_device
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/devices
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{r2_create_a_tenant_for_this_flow.response.body.$.apiKey.key}}

{
  "userId": "user-42",
  "token": "{{FCM_TOKEN}}",
  "platform": "DEVICE_PLATFORM_ANDROID"
}

### 5 · Check the devices
# The token should be listed, active=true.
# Query params: user_id = user-42
# @name r5_check_the_devices
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/devices?user_id=user-42
x-api-key: {{r2_create_a_tenant_for_this_flow.response.body.$.apiKey.key}}

### 6 · Create the push template
# subject = notification title.
# @name r6_create_the_push_template
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/templates
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{r2_create_a_tenant_for_this_flow.response.body.$.apiKey.key}}

{
  "channel": "CHANNEL_PUSH",
  "name": "order-shipped",
  "content": { "subject": "Order shipped", "body": "Order {{orderId}} is on its way" }
}

### 7 · Send push to all the user's devices
# Worker loads the user's tokens → FCM. metadata arrives in the app as the data payload (+
# notificationId). Dead tokens are deactivated.
# @name r7_send_push_to_all_the_user_s_devices
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{r2_create_a_tenant_for_this_flow.response.body.$.apiKey.key}}

{
  "channel": "CHANNEL_PUSH",
  "userId": "user-42",
  "template": "order-shipped",
  "data": { "orderId": "ORD-1001" },
  "metadata": { "deeplink": "app://orders/ORD-1001" }
}

### 8 · Check delivery
# status SENT; provider fcm; providerName firebase.
# Path params: notification id = <NOTIFICATION_ID>  (notification.id from a send)
# @name r8_check_delivery
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications/{{r7_send_push_to_all_the_user_s_devices.response.body.$.notification.id}}
x-api-key: {{r2_create_a_tenant_for_this_flow.response.body.$.apiKey.key}}

### 9 · Send push to one device (no template)
# recipient = the device token.
# @name r9_send_push_to_one_device_no_template
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{r2_create_a_tenant_for_this_flow.response.body.$.apiKey.key}}

{
  "channel": "CHANNEL_PUSH",
  "recipient": "{{FCM_TOKEN}}",
  "subject": "Flash sale",
  "body": "20% off for the next 2 hours",
  "metadata": { "deeplink": "app://sale" }
}

### 10 · Check delivery
# As step 8.
# Path params: notification id = <NOTIFICATION_ID>  (notification.id from a send)
# @name r10_check_delivery
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications/{{r9_send_push_to_one_device_no_template.response.body.$.notification.id}}
x-api-key: {{r2_create_a_tenant_for_this_flow.response.body.$.apiKey.key}}
